"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkjobmetric_document=globalThis.webpackChunkjobmetric_document||[]).push([[8749],{91895(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"introducing-jobic","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/introducing-jobic","editUrl":"https://github.com/jobmetric/document/blog/2026-11-27-introducing-jobic.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-27-introducing-jobic.md","title":"Introducing Jobic: A CMS built on Laravel","description":"Meet JobMetric\'s flagship CMS for teams that want an editorial workspace and a Laravel application they can extend.","date":"2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Jobic","permalink":"/blog/tags/jobic","description":"Product news and guides from the Jobic team."},{"inline":false,"label":"Laravel","permalink":"/blog/tags/laravel","description":"Building websites and applications with Laravel."}],"readingTime":0.95,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"JobMetric Team","url":"https://github.com/jobmetric","key":"jobmetric","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"introducing-jobic","title":"Introducing Jobic: A CMS built on Laravel","description":"Meet JobMetric\'s flagship CMS for teams that want an editorial workspace and a Laravel application they can extend.","authors":["jobmetric"],"tags":["jobic","laravel"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"From draft to publication with Jobic\u2019s editorial workflows","permalink":"/blog/jobic-editorial-workflows"}},"content":"Jobic is JobMetric\'s flagship CMS. It gives editorial teams a workspace for managing content and gives developers a Laravel application they can extend with the same tools they already use.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## A workspace for the people who run the site\\n\\nEditors can write pages and posts with a block editor, preview their drafts, and select assets from a shared media library. Teams working in multiple languages can manage active languages and edit language-specific content. Role-based permissions help teams give editors and administrators access to the work each role handles.\\n\\n## Laravel stays at the center\\n\\nThe application still uses Eloquent for data, Blade for views, Laravel policies for authorization, and Artisan for command-line tasks. When your site needs a custom catalog, a member area, or an integration with another service, your developers can build it using those same conventions.\\n\\nA publishing team might start with posts, media, and editorial review. A business might start with pages and add a catalog later. Both projects can use the same CMS foundation and grow in different directions.\\n\\n[Explore Jobic](/jobic) for a closer look at the workspace, architecture, and setup."},{"id":"jobic-editorial-workflows","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/jobic-editorial-workflows","editUrl":"https://github.com/jobmetric/document/blog/2026-11-27-jobic-editorial-workflows.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-27-jobic-editorial-workflows.md","title":"From draft to publication with Jobic\u2019s editorial workflows","description":"See how Jobic combines the block editor, Kanban, role-based transitions, and workflow simulation.","date":"2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Jobic","permalink":"/blog/tags/jobic","description":"Product news and guides from the Jobic team."}],"readingTime":0.99,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"JobMetric Team","url":"https://github.com/jobmetric","key":"jobmetric","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"jobic-editorial-workflows","title":"From draft to publication with Jobic\u2019s editorial workflows","description":"See how Jobic combines the block editor, Kanban, role-based transitions, and workflow simulation.","authors":["jobmetric"],"tags":["jobic"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Introducing Jobic: A CMS built on Laravel","permalink":"/blog/introducing-jobic"},"nextItem":{"title":"The open-source Laravel packages behind Jobic","permalink":"/blog/open-source-behind-jobic"}},"content":"Publishing gets harder when several people review a post, work across languages, or need to agree on when a draft is ready. Jobic brings that work together with an editor, a content Kanban board, and configurable workflow transitions.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Give each stage a purpose\\n\\nAn author can write and preview a draft, then send it for review when the configured workflow allows it. The Kanban board helps the team see posts by stage. A reviewer can move a post through an available transition, subject to that person\'s role and the workflow\'s rules.\\n\\nA simple workflow might have **Draft**, **Review**, and **Publish** stages. Teams can define stages and transitions around their own editorial process.\\n\\n## Test a workflow before using it with real content\\n\\nJobic\'s workflow designer can simulate an unsaved workflow. Provide a sample draft, choose a stage and role, then inspect which transitions are available and which checks pass. The simulation does not publish the draft or execute workflow actions.\\n\\nStart with one review step that solves a real problem for your team. Test it with two roles, such as author and reviewer, before adding more stages.\\n\\n[See the editorial workspace on the Jobic product page](/jobic)."},{"id":"open-source-behind-jobic","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/open-source-behind-jobic","editUrl":"https://github.com/jobmetric/document/blog/2026-11-27-open-source-behind-jobic.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-27-open-source-behind-jobic.md","title":"The open-source Laravel packages behind Jobic","description":"Meet the JobMetric packages that handle permissions, editorial workflows, and localization in Jobic.","date":"2026-11-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Jobic","permalink":"/blog/tags/jobic","description":"Product news and guides from the Jobic team."},{"inline":false,"label":"Laravel","permalink":"/blog/tags/laravel","description":"Building websites and applications with Laravel."},{"inline":false,"label":"Open source","permalink":"/blog/tags/open-source","description":"Reusable packages and tools from JobMetric."}],"readingTime":0.77,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"JobMetric Team","url":"https://github.com/jobmetric","key":"jobmetric","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"open-source-behind-jobic","title":"The open-source Laravel packages behind Jobic","description":"Meet the JobMetric packages that handle permissions, editorial workflows, and localization in Jobic.","authors":["jobmetric"],"tags":["jobic","laravel","open-source"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"From draft to publication with Jobic\u2019s editorial workflows","permalink":"/blog/jobic-editorial-workflows"}},"content":"Jobic brings several of JobMetric\'s open-source Laravel packages together in one application. You can also use those packages independently when your own Laravel project needs a single capability.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Three capabilities, separate packages\\n\\n- **Rolix** gives Jobic a foundation for role-based permissions. Jobic uses it to enforce access to admin pages and actions.\\n- **Laravel Flow** provides building blocks for stages and transitions. Jobic uses them to model how posts move through editorial review.\\n- **Laravel Language and Laravel Translation** support language records and translatable fields. Jobic uses them in its multilingual content workflow.\\n\\nThis separation gives teams a practical choice. If your existing Laravel app needs workflow states, you can explore Laravel Flow on its own. If you want a CMS with an editorial workspace, media library, and role management, look at how Jobic brings those capabilities together.\\n\\n[Browse JobMetric\u2019s package documentation](/packages/intro) or [see how the packages fit into Jobic](/jobic)."}]}}')}}]);